//0.9.11: a body-less, non-native constructor is still a legal
//declaration (the abstract shape). A zero-argument call to it allocates
//the object without running any constructor body — the same shape as a
//type with no constructor at all — so it stays legal after the candidate
//filter. The field keeps its zero-initialized value.
class Cfg {
    public int x;
    Cfg();
}
int main() {
    Cfg c = Cfg();
    return c.x;
}
